description:
Design a module that computes the two's complement of a given N-bit input. The module takes an N-2 bit wide input, extends it to 2*N bits, and produces a 2*N bit output. The output is calculated by inverting the input bits and adding one, effectively transforming the input into its negative representation in binary format, suitable for arithmetic operations in digital circuits.
module top_module(
        a,
        b
    );

code:
module top_module(
        a,
        b
    );parameter Q = 15;
	parameter N = 32;

    input [N-2:0] a;
    output [2*N-1:0] b;


	reg [2*N-1:0] data;
	reg [2*N-1:0] flip;
	reg [2*N-1:0] out;


	assign b = out;

	always @(a)
	begin
		data <= a;		
	end

	always @(data)
	begin
		flip <= ~a;
	end

	always @(flip)
	begin
		out <= flip + 1;
	end

endmodule

