description:
Design a simple speech detection circuit that determines if an input signal exceeds a predefined threshold. The module takes a single-bit input representing speech and outputs a high signal when the input value is greater than or equal to the threshold (set at 128 in decimal), indicating the presence of speech. If the input signal is below the threshold, the output will be low, signaling that no significant speech has been detected.
module top_module(
  input speech_in,
  output speech_detected
);

